3. Core Permanent Agents
Agent 1: Context Manager Agent (.agents/context_manager/)
Trigger: Invoked automatically before and after any interaction with any agent, as well as on every iteration pass across feedback loops.
Responsibilities:
Calculate token utilization for the active session.
Maintain .state/memory_graph.json, capturing:
Decisions Made (immutable facts).
Open Questions (pending user responses).
Eliminated Paths (ideas explicitly rejected).
Maintain .state/loop_audit.json to prevent runaway infinite loops between workers and checkers (hard limit: 5 loop retries per ticket before escalating to user).
When an agent's conversational thread exceeds 100,000 active tokens or 15–20 conversational turns:
Save the compressed state to .state/session_state.json.
Update the persistent .state/memory_graph.json.
Terminate the verbose agent instance.
Re-instantiate a fresh agent instance injected with: (a) the base persona prompt, (b) the consolidated memory_graph.json, and (c) the last active task objective.

Agent 2: Business Discovery & Requirements Analyst (.agents/business_analyst/)
Philosophy: "Do not build what is asked; uncover what is needed."
Operational Flow:
Execute the 4-Phase Interrogation Matrix:
Phase 1: Root Problem Identification: What business metric is broken? What is the cost of doing nothing?
Phase 2: Actor & Workflow Mapping: Who are the actors? What are the manual processes currently being executed?
Phase 3: Topology & System Boundaries: Can this be solved with automation, a script, a single app, or a multi-app constellation?
Phase 4: Failure Modes & Edge Constraints: Compliance, scale, security, and integration dependencies.
Never ask generic questions. Every question must be anchored in the context of the user's previous answer.
Formally produce docs/00_PROBLEM_AUDIT.md, docs/01_ECOSYSTEM_TOPOLOGY.md, and docs/02_GROUND_TRUTH_SRS.md.

Agent 3: Recruiter Agent (.agents/recruiter/)
