Loop Mechanics & Rules:
Loop A: Worker ⇄ QA Adversary (Test-Driven Verification):
Step 1: Before workers write production code, the QA Adversary derives automated test suites from docs/03_TEST_ACCEPTANCE.md.
Step 2: The Engineering Swarm implements the feature against the test suite.
Step 3: The QA Adversary runs the test suite in the environment. If any assertion fails or regression occurs, the QA Adversary rejects the commit, logs error traces to .state/loop_audit.json, and sends the code back to the worker with explicit failure diffs.
Step 4: Repeat until 100% of acceptance assertions pass.

Loop B: Worker ⇄ DevOps & Security Auditor (Runtime & Infrastructure Verification):
Step 1: Once QA passes, the DevOps Auditor attempts dry-run builds, dependency vulnerability checks, and container/infrastructure orchestration.
Step 2: If build scripts fail, secrets are exposed, or container boot checks timeout, DevOps halts promotion, logs actionable remediation requirements to .state/loop_audit.json, and returns the task to the Engineering Swarm.
Step 3: Worker updates configurations and scripts. DevOps re-tests until build, runtime, and security checks succeed.

Circuit Breaker Protocol:
If any loop reaches 5 consecutive rejections, execution pauses automatically. The Context Manager compiles the loop history and summons the Master Orchestrator / User to resolve the architectural conflict or requirement ambiguity.

5. Model-Specific Tool Handling & Translation
Case A: Running in Claude / Anthropic
Use the raw format directly from alirezarezvani/claude-skills:
{
  "name": "execute_query",
  "description": "Run SQL query on internal DB",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "query": {"type": "string", "description": "The raw SQL statement"}
    },
    "required": ["query"]
  }
}

Case B: Running in Gemini (Transpiled Output in .skills/gemini_adapted/)
import google.generativeai as genai

execute_query_declaration = genai.protos.FunctionDeclaration(
    name="execute_query",
    description="Run SQL query on internal DB",
    parameters=genai.protos.Schema(
        type=genai.protos.Type.OBJECT,
        properties={
            "query": genai.protos.Schema(
                type=genai.protos.Type.STRING,
                description="The raw SQL statement"
            )
        },
        required=["query"]
    )
)

